---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const effective = 'August 14, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — Angel0x1" description="How Angel0x1 handles your data: it stays on your device.">
  <main class="wrap legal">
    <a href="/" class="eyebrow back">← Back</a>
    <p class="soul legal-title">Privacy</p>
    <p class="eyebrow faint">Effective {effective}</p>
    <p class="soft lead">
      The short version: your writing stays on your device, and nothing leaves it
      without your say-so. There is no account, and there is nothing for us to read,
      sell, or lose.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">What stays on your device</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        Your entries, the App’s reflections, moods, embeddings, transcripts, and the
        portrait it builds of you are encrypted on your device with AES-256-GCM. The
        key lives in your device’s Keychain, bound to device unlock, and is never
        transmitted or synced. By default the App makes no network calls, and it has no
        account and no ads.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">On-device AI</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        Reflections are generated by AI running on your phone — Apple’s on-device models
        or an optional model you choose to download. Downloading a model fetches
        software from Apple or Hugging Face; none of your journal content is ever sent
        with it. Voice features use on-device speech recognition — your audio is not sent
        off your device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Purchases</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        Subscriptions are processed by Apple through the App Store, using your Apple ID.
        [Provider Name] never sees or stores your payment details, and can never read
        your journal. The App confirms your purchase on-device to unlock Pro; Apple may
        share only aggregate, anonymous sales statistics with us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Optional features — each off until you turn it on</h2>
      <ul class="soft points">
        <li><strong>Anonymous usage stats:</strong> which screens and features are used — never what you write. Off unless you enable analytics in Settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Referrals &amp; early-access rewards:</strong> use your iCloud identity via Apple’s CloudKit and an opaque code — we don’t receive your name, email, or contacts.</li>
        <li><strong>Health insights:</strong> read on-device only; nothing is transmitted.</li>
        <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> composed on-device. Note that once delivered, the text of a notification is handled by iOS’s notification system, which sits outside the App’s encryption — so keep sensitive previews hidden on your lock screen if that matters to you.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">This website &amp; the waitlist</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        This site sets no tracking cookies, runs no analytics, and loads no third-party
        scripts or fonts. If you join the waitlist, your email is stored only to notify
        you at launch and to grant early-access rewards — never sold, rented, or shared.
        Ask us to delete it anytime by replying to any message we send, or by writing to
        the address below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Your control &amp; deletion</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        You can delete any entry, or erase everything, at any time. “Erase everything”
        performs a cryptographic wipe — your content and its key are destroyed and cannot
        be recovered. Uninstalling the App removes its local data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Children</h2>
      <p class="soft">Angel0x1 is intended for people 17 and older and is not directed to children.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">Changes &amp; contact</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        If this policy materially changes, we’ll post it here and, in the App, ask you to
        review and accept it again. Questions about privacy:
        <a href="mailto:[contact email]" class="ilink">[contact email]</a> ([Provider Name]).
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="eyebrow faint updated">A plain-language summary, not a substitute for legal advice.</p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 680px; padding-block: clamp(120px,16vh,180px) 120px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
  .legal-title { font-size: clamp(40px,7vw,72px); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1; }
  .legal .lead { margin: 10px 0 18px; font-size: 1.05em; }
  .legal section { padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .legal .h3 { font-size: clamp(19px,2.4vw,24px); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .legal .points { margin: 4px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px; }
  .legal .points li { line-height: 1.55; }
  .legal .ilink { color: var(--red); }
  .legal .ilink:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .back { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .updated { margin-top: 34px; }
</style>
